{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789793523,"nonce":"RrxesE4Uw4Dp5h+cinMudwUqz68=","title":"Python: an operation on a value not yet typed decided a list's kind too early","message":"In the first inference round a parameter is Unknown. A subscript or\nslice of it (`board[ip + 1:]`), a list literal or comprehension over\nits elements (`[b for b in board[ip + 1:] if ...]`) and the target of a\nloop over `enumerate(board)` all came out Object rather than Unknown, so\nthe list built from them was decided `List(Object)` in that round; the\nrecursive call passed it back into the parameter, and the join of\n`List(Object)` with the caller's `List(Tuple)` is Object. nqueens'\n`place(board, queens, ...)` ran with both lists dynamic.\n\nFix: a subscript of Unknown is Unknown, a list literal or comprehension\nwhose element is Unknown is Unknown, and `Typer::item_ty` types what one\nround of `range`, `enumerate` or an iterable binds, used by the walker's\n`for`, by comprehension generators (each seeing the earlier targets) and\nby the lowering. `place` is now `(List(Tuple), List(Str), Set, ...)`.","files":null}]}